#!/usr/bin/env bash
# mesh-cam-watch — motion-triggered camera REFLEX: when the frame changes, snap a photo and send it
# to the operator's Telegram. Pure reflex — runs as a systemd --user service, NO minds involved
# (operator 2026-06-19: "на рефлексах, там не должно быть никаких миндов работать"). Lives on a node
# with a webcam (default-string).
#
# HOW: every CAM_POLL seconds grab a frame (fswebcam), compare it to the previous frame as a downscaled
# grayscale mean-absolute-difference (PIL). If the difference exceeds CAM_THRESH (something moved /
# changed in view) and we're past the CAM_COOLDOWN since the last alert, send the full-res frame to
# Telegram and log the event. The first frame just seeds the baseline (no false trigger).
#
#   mesh-cam-watch --daemon    run the watch loop forever (the service ExecStart)
#   mesh-cam-watch --once      one capture+compare cycle (cron-style; persists baseline between runs)
#   mesh-cam-watch --clip-now  record a short clip now and send it to Telegram (manual verb / verify)
#   mesh-cam-watch --noise     measure the static-scene diff (noise floor) → pick a threshold
#   mesh-cam-watch --test      synthetic diff + clip-GIF-assembly test (no camera, no Telegram)
#
# VIDEO-ON-PERSON (CAM_VIDEO=1): on a motion alert, confirm a real person is in frame via the
# mesh-face-recognize reflex (Groq vision — NOT a Claude mind, no tokens), then record a short burst of
# frames, assemble them into an animated GIF (PIL, no ffmpeg) and send it as a looping clip to Telegram.
# CAM_VIDEO_CONFIRM=0 sends on any motion (skip the person gate). Clip: CAM_CLIP_FRAMES=12 · CAM_CLIP_W=480.
#
# LIVENESS/BLINDNESS (2026-07-04): ~/.mesh/.cam-watch.state = SEEING/DARK/COVERED/SHUTTERED/FLAT/CAPTURE-FAIL|stats,
# refreshed every CAM_STATE_EVERY (60s) — mtime = the loop ran a real capture, content = what the lens
# sees; class transitions edge-logged to cam-events.log. Before this, .cam-motion (motion-only stamp)
# was the sole artifact → a lens dark since 06-29 midday was 4.4 days indistinguishable from a still room.
#
# COVERED vs DARK (cam-covered-classifier, discover/health 2026-07-06): a covered lens (shutter/tape/cap)
# reads a FLAT DARK FIELD — mean<30 AND luma stddev≈0 (health measured the live IdeaPad shutter at
# mean=1.03 stddev=0.281 over 307200px). A genuinely dark ROOM the lens still SEES carries real sensor
# noise (stddev ≳ 2). Conflating them (the old DARK) made every cam-dependent sense structurally hollow
# for days — the eye was BLIND but the mesh read "room dark". So the flat-dark subset is now COVERED (the
# dark twin of FLAT's bright obstruction): the eye is blocked, not seeing a dark room. On a >CAM_COVERED_DWELL
# continuous COVERED dwell the loop posts ONE [cam-covered] board line + asks the operator once whether the
#
# EC PRIVACY-KILL gate (2026-07-14, consumes mesh-cam-power's .cam-power-state): a FRESH camera_power=off
# means the operator's Fn privacy key cut the webcam at the EC — COVERED renders SHUTTERED (intentional,
# no [cam-covered] alarm) and CAPTURE-FAIL is annotated campower=off(privacy-kill) (token unchanged, so
# motion-attrib still honestly renders UNKNOWN). Stale/missing power state changes nothing (honest-degrade).
# shutter is intentional; `mesh-cam-watch --shuttered on` sets the operator-intent flag → COVERED renders
# SHUTTERED (known-intentional, silenced) instead of a recurring alarm.
#
# OPERATOR-SEND THROTTLE (operator 2026-07-06, Telegram): "пусть для себя он делает больше фото, а мне
# отправляет максимум одно в час". The motion loop, the .cam-motion occupancy stamp, the room-comment
# poke and the face-rec gate all keep running at their own cadence (CAM_COOLDOWN) — that is the mesh
# sensing FOR ITSELF. But the Telegram delivery TO THE OPERATOR is separately rate-limited to at most one
# every CAM_TG_INTERVAL seconds (default 3600 = 1/hour) via the ~/.mesh/.cam-last-tg stamp, and sends a
# single frame, not the burst. So a busy room no longer floods his chat while the mesh still watches it.
#
# FACE-STATE (gen-pair fusion 2026-07-08, cam-watch × mesh-operator-home): every person_present()
# identity read (Ilya|Rozalia|Stranger|Nobody|?) is also stamped to ~/.mesh/.cam-face-state — a
# `-state`-named artifact, so it is automatically fleet-visible via mesh-fleet-states with zero extra
# wiring. This gives a vision-based "who is physically in THIS room" fact that no phone/BLE/LAN axis
# carries; mesh-operator-home's SIGNAL 5 reads it cross-node as AWAY counter-evidence (a phone dark on
# every axis but the camera just recognized Ilya in frame ≠ the operator left).
#
# Tunables (env): CAM_DEV=/dev/video0 · CAM_POLL=1.5 · CAM_THRESH=14 · CAM_COOLDOWN=15 · CAM_WARMUP=8
#   CAM_RES=1280x720 · CAM_CHAT=<override chat_id> · CAM_VIDEO=1 · CAM_PHOTOS=0 · CAM_STATE_EVERY=60
#   CAM_TG_INTERVAL=3600 (min seconds between operator-facing Telegram sends) · CAM_BURST=4.
#   Creds: ~/.config/remote-access/env.
#
# ── SENSORIMOTOR-CONTINGENCY GAP: this eye is a PASSIVE snapshot; liveness is never ACTED-into ──
# LITERATURE (enaction / biology of cognition — live review, genome mind, 2026-07-21, WebSearch).
# Concept: SENSORIMOTOR CONTINGENCY THEORY — J. Kevin O'Regan & Alva Noë, "A sensorimotor account of
# vision and visual consciousness" (Behavioral & Brain Sciences 24(5), 2001), the enactive lineage of
# Maturana/Varela → Varela/Thompson/Rosch (*The Embodied Mind*). Its claim: perceiving is NOT receiving
# a picture; it is the exercise of MASTERY of sensorimotor contingencies — the LAWFUL ways the sensory
# input covaries with the perceiver's OWN action. A quality is perceived BECAUSE the agent implicitly
# knows how the reading would change if it moved/acted. Formalized and kept live by Buhrmann, Di Paolo &
# Barandiaran, "A dynamical systems account of sensorimotor contingencies" (Frontiers in Psychology 4:285,
# 2013) and carried forward in the SMC-learning robotics literature (2024/25). Verified absent from this
# genome (no "sensorimotor"/"O'Regan"/"Noë" anywhere) before landing — WebSearch + tree grep 2026-07-21.
# Where THIS reflex stops short: the whole SEEING/DARK/COVERED/SHUTTERED/FLAT taxonomy above classifies
# frame STATISTICS (mean, luma stddev, frame-to-frame mean-abs-diff) — a purely RECEPTIVE read. It has no
# FROZEN class, and that is the structural hole: a driver returning a CACHED/STUCK frame (uvcvideo wedge,
# a looped fake, a hung capture that re-serves the last good buffer) yields IDENTICAL bytes every poll →
# healthy mean, healthy stddev, motion-diff ≈ 0 → classified SEEING as a "calm live room". A genuinely
# live lens on a static scene NEVER reads diff==0 (thermal/shot noise floats every pixel; --noise already
# measures that floor) — but "diff below noise floor for a long dwell" is exactly what a passive stat
# CANNOT disambiguate from "nothing is moving". This is the hollow-sense failure the verification doctrine
# fights (mesh-mag/mesh-gyro dead-but-green, the EYES USB-cam wedge) named at its root: we test that a
# fresh, statistically-plausible artifact ARRIVED, never that the reading RESPONDS LAWFULLY TO ACTION.
# CONCRETE APPLICATION (proposed, NOT shipped — needs the live Note3 cam+torch pairing to calibrate):
# an SMC liveness PROBE. On the ambiguous SEEING-but-diff≈0 dwell, ACTUATE the co-located rear flash
# (`termux-torch on` — already a mesh primitive: mesh-ear:86, mesh-act:481, genius-loci, mesh-converse)
# for one capture and assert frame mean-luma RISES by > the --noise floor, then torch off and assert it
# FALLS back. A lawful luminance response ⟹ the pixels are live (SMC satisfied); NO response ⟹ FROZEN —
# a hollow class the passive mean/stddev/diff taxonomy structurally cannot emit. Read-only/off-by-default
# first (log the Δluma, confirm it LEADS real freezes) BEFORE it gates .cam-watch.state — same cry-wolf,
# instrument-first caution as mesh-body-power's held --trajectory. Honest-degrade: torchless node / dark
# room where the flash can't reach the scene ⟹ probe returns UNKNOWN, never a faked FROZEN nor a faked
# SEEING. DISTINCT from the landed neighbours: NOT COVERED/FLAT (those are obstruction stats of ONE frame)
# and NOT the passive noise-floor threshold pick (--noise) — SMC adds the ACTION→reading law those lack.
set -uo pipefail
export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"

CAM_DEV="${CAM_DEV:-/dev/video0}"
CAM_POLL="${CAM_POLL:-1.5}"
CAM_THRESH="${CAM_THRESH:-14}"        # mean abs grayscale diff (0-255) that counts as motion
CAM_COOLDOWN="${CAM_COOLDOWN:-15}"    # min seconds between sent alerts (anti-spam)
CAM_WARMUP="${CAM_WARMUP:-8}"         # fswebcam frames to skip for exposure
CAM_RES="${CAM_RES:-1280x720}"
# Use the REAL curl, never a snap-confined one: ds has a `curl` snap that, under the systemd --user
# service, shadows /usr/bin/curl on PATH. A snap curl can't read hidden dirs (~/.mesh) or the private
# /tmp → it fails every photo upload with exit 26 (read error) while plain-shell curl works. That was
# the real "motion photos never arrive" cause (NOT a network blip). Prefer the unconfined binary.
CURL="${CAM_CURL:-/usr/bin/curl}"; [ -x "$CURL" ] || CURL="curl"
MESH="${MESH_DIR:-$HOME/.mesh}"
PREV="$MESH/cam-prev.jpg"
LASTF="$MESH/cam-last-alert"
LOG="$MESH/cam-events.log"
STATE="$MESH/.cam-watch.state"        # liveness+blindness artifact: SEEING/DARK/COVERED/SHUTTERED/FLAT/CAPTURE-FAIL
CAM_STATE_EVERY="${CAM_STATE_EVERY:-60}"  # seconds between state refreshes (poll is ~1.5s; stats hourly-rate)
CAM_TG_INTERVAL="${CAM_TG_INTERVAL:-3600}"  # min seconds between OPERATOR-facing Telegram sends (default 1/hour)
TGSTAMP="$MESH/.cam-last-tg"          # last time anything was delivered to the operator's Telegram
# COVERED-lens (cam-covered-classifier): the flat-dark discriminator + the >dwell one-shot operator alert.
CAM_COVERED_SD="${CAM_COVERED_SD:-1.5}"       # luma stddev below this (AND mean<30) = COVERED, not DARK.
                                              # health-calibrated: live shutter sd=0.281, a dark room sd≳2.
CAM_COVERED_DWELL="${CAM_COVERED_DWELL:-3600}" # continuous-COVERED seconds before the ONE board+tg alert
CAM_COVERED_TG="${CAM_COVERED_TG:-1}"         # 1 = also ask the operator once via Telegram; 0 = board-only
COVSINCE="$MESH/.cam-covered-since"   # "<epoch_covered_began> <announced 0|1>" — cleared when the lens opens
INTENT_FLAG="$MESH/.cam-shutter-intended"  # presence = operator confirmed the shutter is INTENTIONALLY closed
# EC privacy-kill disambiguator (mesh-cam-power, 300956f): camera_power=off means the operator's Fn
# privacy key cut the webcam's power at the EC — /dev/video* still enumerate but capture is black or
# fails outright. Consuming it here closes the link the cam-power header promises: a COVERED frame or
# CAPTURE-FAIL with power=off is EXPECTED (intentional shutter, hardware edition), not a lens/driver fault.
CAMPOWER_STATE="$MESH/.cam-power-state"    # mesh-cam-power artifact: "on"|"off"|"<raw>"; mtime = ran-live
CAMPOWER_FRESH="${CAM_POWER_FRESH:-1800}"  # producer cadence */10 — 3x = stale, stop trusting it

# ec_privacy_kill — 0 iff mesh-cam-power's state is FRESH and reads 'off'. Missing/stale/on/raw →
# non-zero: we never claim privacy-kill without a fresh EC read (honest-degrade — a stale 'off'
# must not silence a real covered-lens alarm forever).
ec_privacy_kill() {
  [ -f "$CAMPOWER_STATE" ] || return 1
  [ $(( $(date +%s) - $(stat -c %Y "$CAMPOWER_STATE" 2>/dev/null || echo 0) )) -le "$CAMPOWER_FRESH" ] || return 1
  [ "$(head -1 "$CAMPOWER_STATE" 2>/dev/null | tr -d '[:space:]')" = off ]
}

# operator-send throttle: 0 = a send is due (past CAM_TG_INTERVAL since the last one), 1 = suppress.
# Separate from CAM_COOLDOWN (which paces the internal motion actions) — this ONLY gates the TG delivery.
tg_send_due() {
  local last=0 nowt; nowt="$(date +%s)"; [ -f "$TGSTAMP" ] && last="$(cat "$TGSTAMP" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)"
  [ $(( nowt - last )) -ge "$CAM_TG_INTERVAL" ]
}
tg_stamp() { date +%s > "$TGSTAMP" 2>/dev/null || true; }
mkdir -p "$MESH" 2>/dev/null || true

# ---- diff helper (PIL): prints the mean-abs grayscale difference between two JPEGs ------------------
diff_metric() {  # <a.jpg> <b.jpg> -> float on stdout (0 if either unreadable → safe no-trigger)
  python3 - "$1" "$2" <<'PY'
import sys
from PIL import Image
try:
    a=Image.open(sys.argv[1]).convert("L").resize((160,120))
    b=Image.open(sys.argv[2]).convert("L").resize((160,120))
    pa=list(a.getdata()); pb=list(b.getdata())
    d=sum(abs(x-y) for x,y in zip(pa,pb))/len(pa)
    print(f"{d:.2f}")
except Exception:
    print("0.00")
PY
}

capture() {  # <out.jpg> -> 0 if a non-empty JPEG was produced
  local cmd="fswebcam --no-banner -d '$CAM_DEV' -r '$CAM_RES' -S '$CAM_WARMUP' '$1'"
  eval "$cmd" >/dev/null 2>&1
  # The ambient context may lack the `video` group (cron/systemd-user started before the group was
  # added → EACCES on /dev/video*). fswebcam then fails but exits 0-ish, so the sense goes SILENTLY
  # dead. Retry once explicitly acquiring the group via `sg` — mirrors mesh-misha-wake's grab_frame.
  [ -s "$1" ] || { command -v sg >/dev/null 2>&1 && sg video -c "$cmd" >/dev/null 2>&1; }
  [ -s "$1" ]
}

send_photo() {  # <jpg> <caption>
  local env="$HOME/.config/remote-access/env"
  [ -f "$env" ] && { set -a; . "$env" 2>/dev/null; set +a; }
  local chat="${CAM_CHAT:-${CHAT_ID:-}}"
  [ -n "${BOT_TOKEN:-}" ] && [ -n "$chat" ] || { echo "send: no BOT_TOKEN/CHAT_ID" >&2; return 1; }
  # NB: NEVER `curl | grep -q` here — the script runs `set -o pipefail`, and grep-q closing the pipe
  # early SIGPIPEs curl → the pipeline returns non-zero EVEN WHEN the photo was delivered (false
  # SEND-FAILED; root cause of the 2026-06-19 "motion photos never arrive" — they DID arrive). Capture
  # the response to a var and substring-test instead. Retry 3x for a genuine transient network blip.
  local i resp rc
  for i in 1 2 3; do
    resp="$("$CURL" -s --max-time 30 "https://api.telegram.org/bot${BOT_TOKEN}/sendPhoto" \
      -F "chat_id=${chat}" -F "photo=@${1}" -F "caption=${2}" 2>>"$MESH/cam-curl.err")"
    rc=$?
    printf '%sZ try=%d curl_rc=%d file=%s(%s b) resp=%.90s\n' "$(date -u +%H:%M:%S)" "$i" "$rc" \
      "$(basename "$1")" "$(stat -c%s "$1" 2>/dev/null)" "$resp" >> "$MESH/cam-send-debug.log" 2>/dev/null
    case "$resp" in *'"ok":true'*) return 0;; esac
    sleep 2
  done
  return 1
}

send_animation() {  # <gif> <caption>  — Telegram renders a sent GIF as an inline looping video
  local env="$HOME/.config/remote-access/env"
  [ -f "$env" ] && { set -a; . "$env" 2>/dev/null; set +a; }
  local chat="${CAM_CHAT:-${CHAT_ID:-}}"
  [ -n "${BOT_TOKEN:-}" ] && [ -n "$chat" ] || { echo "send: no BOT_TOKEN/CHAT_ID" >&2; return 1; }
  # Same pipefail-safe pattern as send_photo: capture resp to a var, substring-test, retry transient blips.
  local i resp
  for i in 1 2 3; do
    resp="$("$CURL" -s --max-time 60 "https://api.telegram.org/bot${BOT_TOKEN}/sendAnimation" \
      -F "chat_id=${chat}" -F "animation=@${1};type=image/gif" -F "caption=${2}" 2>>"$MESH/cam-curl.err")"
    printf '%sZ video try=%d file=%s(%s b) resp=%.90s\n' "$(date -u +%H:%M:%S)" "$i" \
      "$(basename "$1")" "$(stat -c%s "$1" 2>/dev/null)" "$resp" >> "$MESH/cam-send-debug.log" 2>/dev/null
    case "$resp" in *'"ok":true'*) return 0;; esac
    sleep 2
  done
  return 1
}

# person gate (operator 2026-06-26 "пусть убедится, что человек"): confirm a real person is in frame
# before spending a clip, via the existing mesh-face-recognize reflex (Groq vision = metabolism inference,
# NOT a Claude mind → no tokens). echoes the label; rc 0 = a human is present, 1 = Nobody, 2 = unknown/err.
person_present() {  # <jpg>
  local who
  who="$(mesh-face-recognize "$1" 2>/dev/null | tr -d '\r' | tail -n1)"
  case "$who" in
    Ilya|Rozalia|Stranger) echo "$who"; return 0;;
    Nobody)                 echo "Nobody"; return 1;;
    *)                      echo "${who:-?}"; return 2;;
  esac
}

# record_clip — capture a short burst of frames (fswebcam) and assemble an animated GIF (PIL, NO ffmpeg
# needed — ds has neither system ffmpeg nor imageio_ffmpeg). Telegram shows it as a looping video clip.
record_clip() {  # <out.gif> -> 0 if a multi-frame GIF was produced
  local out="$1" n="${CAM_CLIP_FRAMES:-12}" w="${CAM_CLIP_W:-480}" dur="${CAM_CLIP_MS:-160}"
  local skip="${CAM_CLIP_SKIP:-2}" delay="${CAM_CLIP_DELAY:-0.2}"
  local dir; dir="$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}"/cam-clip-XXXXXX)"
  local i f got=0
  for i in $(seq 1 "$n"); do
    f="$dir/f$(printf '%02d' "$i").jpg"
    local ccmd="fswebcam --no-banner -d '$CAM_DEV' -r '$CAM_RES' -S '$skip' '$f'"
    eval "$ccmd" >/dev/null 2>&1
    # same video-group EACCES retry as capture() — a group-less ambient must not silently drop frames
    [ -s "$f" ] || { command -v sg >/dev/null 2>&1 && sg video -c "$ccmd" >/dev/null 2>&1; }
    [ -s "$f" ] && got=$((got+1))
    sleep "$delay"
  done
  [ "$got" -ge 2 ] || { rm -rf "$dir"; return 1; }
  python3 - "$out" "$w" "$dur" "$dir"/*.jpg <<'PY'
import sys
from PIL import Image
out=sys.argv[1]; w=int(sys.argv[2]); dur=int(sys.argv[3]); paths=sys.argv[4:]
frames=[]
for p in paths:
    try: im=Image.open(p).convert("RGB")
    except Exception: continue
    if im.width>w:
        im=im.resize((w,int(im.height*w/im.width)))
    frames.append(im)
if len(frames)<2: sys.exit(1)
frames[0].save(out, save_all=True, append_images=frames[1:], duration=dur, loop=0, optimize=True)
sys.exit(0)
PY
  local rc=$?; rm -rf "$dir"; [ "$rc" -eq 0 ] && [ -s "$out" ]
}

log_evt() { printf '%sZ  %s\n' "$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S)" "$1" >> "$LOG" 2>/dev/null || true; }

# FACE-STATE (gen-pair fusion, cam-watch × mesh-operator-home): every person_present() identity read
# is a vision-based "who is physically in THIS room" fact that no phone/BLE/LAN signal carries. Stamp
# it as a `-state` artifact (the fleet's standard liveness-touch shape: content=value, mtime=freshness,
# consumed fleet-wide over SSH by mesh-fleet-states with zero extra wiring) so a consumer on another
# node (mesh-operator-home SIGNAL 5) can read "was Ilya recognized recently, on which node" without
# re-implementing face-rec. Fires on every face-rec call, independent of the TG send-throttle/cooldown
# gates below — this is the mesh sensing FOR ITSELF, same split as .cam-motion.
FACE_STATE="$MESH/.cam-face-state"
face_state_write() {  # <who>  (Ilya|Rozalia|Stranger|Nobody|?)
  printf '%s\n' "$1" > "$FACE_STATE.tmp" 2>/dev/null && mv -f "$FACE_STATE.tmp" "$FACE_STATE" 2>/dev/null
}

# ---- liveness+blindness state (2026-07-04, the 4.4-day hollow) --------------------------------------
# The daemon's only artifact used to be .cam-motion — stamped ON MOTION ONLY — so a covered/dark lens
# (real case: dark even at midday since 06-29 12:24), a dead camera, or a genuinely still room were all
# the same eternal silence: systemd green, zero record, nothing alarmed. Per the liveness-touch
# convention: .cam-watch.state mtime = the loop ran a real capture (refreshed every CAM_STATE_EVERY s),
# content = what the lens sees. Class TRANSITIONS are edge-logged to cam-events.log so "when did the
# lens go dark" is answerable after the fact.
frame_class() {  # <jpg> <diff> [covered_sd] -> CLASS|diff=..|mean=..|span=..|sd=..
                 # CLASS: SEEING / DARK / COVERED / FLAT / STAT-FAIL
  python3 - "$1" "$2" "${3:-$CAM_COVERED_SD}" <<'PY'
import sys
from PIL import Image
try:
    # NEAREST resample: subsample, do NOT smooth — smoothing (bicubic default) averages away the very
    # sensor-noise variance that separates a COVERED flat field (sd≈0) from a DARK room the eye SEES
    # (sd≳2). The covered discriminator is a variance read, so it must survive the downscale.
    im=Image.open(sys.argv[1]).convert("L").resize((160,120), Image.NEAREST)
    raw=list(im.getdata()); n=len(raw)
    mean=sum(raw)/n
    var=sum((p-mean)**2 for p in raw)/n
    sd=var**0.5
    covered_sd=float(sys.argv[3])
    px=sorted(raw)
    span=px[int(n*0.98)]-px[int(n*0.02)]   # p2-p98 spread: ignores stuck pixels
    if mean<30 and sd<covered_sd:
        cls="COVERED"                       # flat DARK field: shutter/tape/cap — the eye is BLIND, not a dark room
    elif span<12 and mean<30:
        cls="DARK"                          # near-black but with real sensor noise/structure: unlit room, eye SEES
    elif span<12:
        cls="FLAT"                          # uniform but lit: lens blocked by a bright obstruction
    else:
        cls="SEEING"
    print(f"{cls}|diff={sys.argv[2]}|mean={mean:.0f}|span={span}|sd={sd:.2f}")
except Exception:
    print("STAT-FAIL|diff=%s"%sys.argv[2])
PY
}

# cam_board — edge board post (best-effort, WHO-tagged). covered_overlay's alert path uses it.
cam_board() { command -v mesh-chat >/dev/null 2>&1 && MESH_WHO="cam-watch@$(hostname)" mesh-chat "$1" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true; }

# covered_overlay <cls> [jpg] -> effective class on stdout. Two jobs, both hermetically testable:
#   (1) operator-intent overlay: a COVERED frame renders SHUTTERED when the operator has confirmed the
#       shutter is intentionally closed (INTENT_FLAG present) — known-intentional, not an alarm.
#   (2) dwell alert: track continuous-COVERED time in COVSINCE; the FIRST cycle past CAM_COVERED_DWELL
#       fires exactly ONE [cam-covered] board line (+ optional tg-ask), guarded by the announced flag so
#       it never repeats within an episode. Any non-COVERED frame clears COVSINCE (resets the episode).
covered_overlay() {
  local cls="$1" jpg="${2:-}" now; now="$(date +%s)"
  if [ "$cls" != COVERED ]; then
    rm -f "$COVSINCE" 2>/dev/null || true          # left the covered state → reset dwell + announce
    printf '%s' "$cls"; return 0
  fi
  if [ -e "$INTENT_FLAG" ]; then                    # operator says it's on purpose → SHUTTERED, no dwell alarm
    printf 'SHUTTERED'; return 0
  fi
  if ec_privacy_kill; then                          # EC camera_power=off: the Fn privacy key IS operator
    printf 'SHUTTERED'; return 0                    # intent, hardware edition → SHUTTERED, no dwell alarm
  fi
  local since="" ann=""
  [ -f "$COVSINCE" ] && read -r since ann < "$COVSINCE" 2>/dev/null
  [[ "${since:-}" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]] || { since="$now"; ann=0; }
  [[ "${ann:-}" =~ ^[01]$ ]] || ann=0
  if [ "$ann" != 1 ] && [ $(( now - since )) -ge "$CAM_COVERED_DWELL" ]; then
    local mins=$(( (now - since) / 60 ))
    cam_board "[cam-covered] $(hostname) camera lens BLIND ${mins}min+ (flat dark field mean<30 sd<${CAM_COVERED_SD}: shutter/tape/cap — NOT a dark room). Cam-dependent senses (color-temp/misha-gate/tempo/room-sense) degraded. If intentional: 'mesh-cam-watch --shuttered on' → renders SHUTTERED, silences."
    if [ "$CAM_COVERED_TG" = 1 ]; then
      if [ -n "$jpg" ] && [ -s "$jpg" ] && command -v send_photo >/dev/null 2>&1; then
        send_photo "$jpg" "👁️‍🗨️ Камера ослепла (${mins}мин+): плоское тёмное поле — шторка закрыта/заклеена? Если специально: mesh-cam-watch --shuttered on" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
      fi
      tg_stamp
    fi
    ann=1
  fi
  printf '%s %s\n' "$since" "$ann" > "$COVSINCE" 2>/dev/null || true
  printf 'COVERED'
}

state_update() {  # <FRAME|CAPTURE-FAIL> <diff> [jpg]  — throttled; atomic write; touch = ran-live
  local due=1 prev_class="" new cls
  if [ -f "$STATE" ]; then
    prev_class="$(cut -d'|' -f1 "$STATE" 2>/dev/null)"
    [ $(( $(date +%s) - $(stat -c %Y "$STATE" 2>/dev/null || echo 0) )) -lt "$CAM_STATE_EVERY" ] && due=0
  fi
  if [ "$1" = CAPTURE-FAIL ]; then
    # annotate the CAUSE when the EC privacy kill explains the failure (token stays CAPTURE-FAIL —
    # consumers like mesh-motion-attrib key on field 1 and must still render UNKNOWN: the lens
    # genuinely cannot see, it's just not a FAULT).
    if ec_privacy_kill; then
      new="CAPTURE-FAIL|dev=$CAM_DEV|campower=off(privacy-kill)"
    else
      new="CAPTURE-FAIL|dev=$CAM_DEV"
    fi
  else
    [ "$due" = 1 ] || return 0        # skip the PIL stats pass on off-cycles
    new="$(frame_class "$3" "$2")" || return 0
    # COVERED overlay: SHUTTERED if operator-intended, + the >dwell one-shot [cam-covered] alert. Rewrites
    # only the class token, preserving the stats tail. (Runs on the throttled due-cycle, so at most 1/min.)
    local _eff; _eff="$(covered_overlay "${new%%|*}" "$3")"
    new="$_eff|${new#*|}"
  fi
  cls="${new%%|*}"
  if [ "$due" = 1 ] || [ "$cls" != "$prev_class" ]; then
    printf '%s\n' "$new" > "$STATE.tmp" 2>/dev/null && mv -f "$STATE.tmp" "$STATE" 2>/dev/null
    mesh-state-touch "$STATE" 2>/dev/null || touch "$STATE" 2>/dev/null || true
    [ -n "$prev_class" ] && [ "$cls" != "$prev_class" ] && log_evt "cam state $prev_class→$cls (${new#*|})"
  fi
  return 0
}

# one cycle: capture → compare to baseline → maybe alert → update baseline. echoes the diff value.
cycle() {
  local now; now="$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}"/cam-now-XXXX.jpg)"
  if ! capture "$now"; then state_update CAPTURE-FAIL "-"; echo "CAPTURE_FAIL"; rm -f "$now"; return 1; fi
  local d="0.00"
  if [ -f "$PREV" ]; then
    d="$(diff_metric "$PREV" "$now")"
    # awk float compare; trigger if d >= THRESH and cooldown elapsed
    if awk "BEGIN{exit !($d>=$CAM_THRESH)}"; then
      # OCCUPANCY SIGNAL (2026-06-21): record EVERY motion detection — BEFORE the alert cooldown gate —
      # so mesh-room-sense has a phone-INDEPENDENT local PRESENT proof (camera saw movement in the room).
      # The cooldown below only throttles the room-comment poke, not this freshness stamp.
      date +%s > "$MESH/.cam-motion" 2>/dev/null || true
      local last=0 nowt; nowt="$(date +%s)"; [ -f "$LASTF" ] && last="$(cat "$LASTF" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)"
      if [ $(( nowt - last )) -ge "$CAM_COOLDOWN" ]; then
        echo "$nowt" > "$LASTF"
        # MOTION AS A ROOM SIGNAL (operator 2026-06-20): movement in the room → let the room mind comment
        # on what's currently being heard. mesh-overhear --poke-mind --motion self-gates: it only speaks
        # when a real conversation is live (fresh transcript) and not more than once per its own cooldown,
        # so continuous movement in a quiet room never makes the mesh blurt. Async; opt-out via CAM_ROOM=0.
        [ "${CAM_ROOM:-1}" = 1 ] && mesh-overhear --poke-mind --motion >/dev/null 2>&1 &
        # EYE-CONTACT WIRING (sense-liveness 2026-07-10): mesh-misha-eye-contact's own header has claimed
        # since 2026-07-04 that "mesh-cam-watch's motion loop hands it a throwaway COPY of the frame it
        # just captured" — that call was never actually added here, so the --frame path it documents as
        # its REAL trigger has been dead code for 6 days (misha-eye.log: 0 bytes since creation). The only
        # thing invoking the tool was a stray standalone-fallback cron entry the tool's own header says was
        # explicitly REJECTED by the operator twice ("timers are bad practice"). Wire the documented path
        # for real: hand off a disposable copy (the contract: --frame consumes/removes its argument, $now
        # is being rm'd by this function regardless). Same cooldown/async/opt-out shape as CAM_ROOM above.
        if [ "${CAM_MISHA_EYE:-1}" = 1 ]; then
          local eyecopy; eyecopy="$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}"/misha-eye-XXXX.jpg)"
          # the rm rides INSIDE the background subshell: the contract says --frame consumes its
          # argument, but a consumer that is absent, errors, or is killed leaves the copy behind —
          # once per motion event, on a poll loop (task:doctor-test-tmpdir-cleanup-traps).
          ( cp -f "$now" "$eyecopy" 2>/dev/null && mesh-misha-eye-contact --frame "$eyecopy" >/dev/null 2>&1
            rm -f "$eyecopy" ) &
        fi
        # VIDEO ON PERSON (operator 2026-06-26, Telegram): "каждый раз когда замечает кого-нибудь / движение —
        # делает видео и шлёт в телегу, но рефлексами, чтобы токены не тратились". On a motion alert, confirm a
        # real person is in frame (person_present → mesh-face-recognize, Groq vision, NOT a Claude mind → no
        # tokens), then record a short clip and send it. Synchronous on purpose: a second concurrent fswebcam
        # would fight the poll loop for /dev/video0 — the ~15s cooldown covers the brief block. Enable: CAM_VIDEO=1.
        # The person gate (face-rec) always runs — it feeds the mesh's own who-is-here signal — but the
        # clip is only recorded+delivered to the operator when the hourly TG window is open.
        if [ "${CAM_VIDEO:-0}" = 1 ]; then
          local who="?" ok_person=1 pr clip
          if [ "${CAM_VIDEO_CONFIRM:-1}" = 1 ]; then
            who="$(person_present "$now")"; pr=$?
            face_state_write "$who"
            [ "$pr" -eq 1 ] && { ok_person=0; log_evt "motion diff=$d — face-rec=Nobody, no clip"; }
          fi
          if [ "$ok_person" = 1 ] && tg_send_due; then
            clip="$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}"/cam-clip-XXXXXX.gif)"
            if record_clip "$clip"; then
              send_animation "$clip" "👁 $who в комнате — $(date '+%H:%M:%S') (движение diff=$d)" \
                && { tg_stamp; log_evt "VIDEO sent who=$who diff=$d ($(stat -c%s "$clip" 2>/dev/null)b)"; } \
                || log_evt "VIDEO who=$who SEND-FAILED"
            else log_evt "VIDEO record FAILED who=$who"; fi
            rm -f "$clip"
          elif [ "$ok_person" = 1 ]; then log_evt "motion diff=$d who=$who (TG throttled, no clip)"; fi
        fi
        # Telegram photos — operator 2026-07-06: at most ONE per CAM_TG_INTERVAL (1/hour), a single frame,
        # not the old 4-burst. Motion detection + cam-prev.jpg + the room poke above still flow every
        # cooldown (the mesh sensing for itself); only the operator delivery is throttled. Off: CAM_PHOTOS=0.
        if [ "${CAM_PHOTOS:-1}" = 1 ] && tg_send_due; then
          local ts; ts="$(date '+%H:%M:%S')"
          send_photo "$now" "🚶 Движение — $ts (diff=$d, макс. 1/час)" \
            && { tg_stamp; log_evt "ALERT diff=$d photo sent (1/${CAM_TG_INTERVAL}s)"; } \
            || log_evt "ALERT diff=$d photo SEND-FAILED"
        elif [ "${CAM_PHOTOS:-1}" = 1 ]; then log_evt "motion diff=$d (TG throttled ${CAM_TG_INTERVAL}s; room-comment poked)"
        else log_evt "motion diff=$d (photos off; room-comment poked)"; fi
      else log_evt "motion diff=$d (cooldown, not sent)"; fi
    fi
  fi
  state_update FRAME "$d" "$now"
  cp -f "$now" "$PREV" 2>/dev/null; rm -f "$now"
  echo "$d"
}

case "${1:-}" in
  --test)
    command -v python3 >/dev/null && python3 -c 'import PIL' 2>/dev/null || { echo "smoke-test: n/a (no PIL)"; exit 2; }
    python3 - <<'PY'
from PIL import Image
import sys, tempfile, os, shutil, signal
# SIGTERM MUST UNWIND, or the `finally` below is decorative: python's DEFAULT SIGTERM disposition
# kills the interpreter WITHOUT running finally blocks, and GNU `timeout` wraps every --test in
# mesh-doctor's hourly sweep, signalling the whole process group. sys.exit() from the handler
# raises SystemExit in the main thread, which is what unwinds. SIGKILL stays uncatchable
# (mesh-tmp-guard's sweep). Pattern: eb5b8e7, scripts/mesh-spend.
for _sig in (signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGHUP):
    signal.signal(_sig, lambda _s, _f: sys.exit(128 + _s))
d=tempfile.mkdtemp()
# This block used to have NO removal at all — it leaked a jpg/gif-bearing temp dir on EVERY --test
# run, signalled or not (mesh-tmp-guard --unwind-scan class `no-cleanup`). The exits below are
# SystemExit, so the cleanup has to be a `finally`, not a trailing statement.
try:
    a=os.path.join(d,"a.jpg"); b=os.path.join(d,"b.jpg"); c=os.path.join(d,"c.jpg")
    Image.new("L",(640,480),100).save(a)               # flat grey
    Image.new("L",(640,480),100).save(b)               # identical
    img=Image.new("L",(640,480),100)                    # grey with a bright block (a "person")
    for y in range(120,360):
        for x in range(200,440): img.putpixel((x,y),230)
    img.save(c)
    def mad(p,q):
        A=Image.open(p).convert("L").resize((160,120)); B=Image.open(q).convert("L").resize((160,120))
        pa=list(A.getdata()); pb=list(B.getdata()); return sum(abs(x-y) for x,y in zip(pa,pb))/len(pa)
    same=mad(a,b); changed=mad(a,c)
    # clip path: assemble a 3-frame animated GIF (PIL, no ffmpeg) and re-read its frame count
    g=os.path.join(d,"clip.gif")
    fr=[Image.new("RGB",(120,90),(i*70,0,0)) for i in (1,2,3)]
    fr[0].save(g, save_all=True, append_images=fr[1:], duration=150, loop=0, optimize=True)
    G=Image.open(g); nf=getattr(G,"n_frames",1); gsz=os.path.getsize(g)
    ok = same<1.0 and changed>14.0 and nf==3 and gsz>0
    print(f"  identical-frames diff={same:.2f} (want <1)  changed-frame diff={changed:.2f} (want >14)")
    print(f"  clip-gif frames={nf} (want 3)  size={gsz}b (want >0)")
    sys.exit(0 if ok else 1)
finally:
    shutil.rmtree(d, ignore_errors=True)
PY
    [ $? -eq 0 ] || { echo "smoke-test: FAIL"; exit 1; }
    # frame_class fixtures (pure PIL, no camera): the blindness classifier behind .cam-watch.state.
    # cam-covered-classifier: the discriminator is VARIANCE — a COVERED flat field (sd≈0, the live shutter
    # health measured at sd=0.281) vs a DARK room the eye still SEES (real sensor noise sd≳2). Both near-black.
    _fcdir="$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}"/cam-fc-XXXXXX)"
    python3 - "$_fcdir" <<'PY'
from PIL import Image
import sys, random
d=sys.argv[1]
Image.new("L",(640,480),15).save(d+"/covered.jpg")   # FLAT dark field sd~0 → COVERED (lens blocked)
# DARK room: near-black but the eye SEES faint STRUCTURE (furniture silhouettes / gradient), sd≳1.5,
# span<12. NOTE: JPEG DCT-quantizes away per-pixel WHITE noise (a gauss(σ=2.5) field collapses to sd~1.3
# post-encode) — so a realistic DARK discriminator must be LOW-FREQUENCY structure, which JPEG preserves.
dk=Image.new("L",(640,480))                           # smooth ramp 10..21: sd~3, span~10 (<12), mean~15
dk.putdata([10 + (x*11)//640 for y in range(480) for x in range(640)])
dk.save(d+"/dark.jpg")
Image.new("L",(640,480),200).save(d+"/flat.jpg")     # bright uniform obstruction → FLAT
img=Image.new("L",(640,480),60)                       # structured scene → SEEING
for y in range(100,380):
    for x in range(150,490): img.putpixel((x,y),210)
img.save(d+"/scene.jpg")
PY
    _fc_fail=0
    for _f in covered:COVERED dark:DARK flat:FLAT scene:SEEING; do
      _cls="$(frame_class "$_fcdir/${_f%%:*}.jpg" 0.00 | cut -d'|' -f1)"
      [ "$_cls" = "${_f##*:}" ] || { echo "  FAIL: frame_class(${_f%%:*}) → $_cls (want ${_f##*:})"; _fc_fail=1; }
    done
    # FALSIFY the split both ways: the flat field must NOT read DARK (else the eye stays hollow), and the
    # noisy dark room must NOT read COVERED (else a real dark room is wrongly called blind).
    _cov="$(frame_class "$_fcdir/covered.jpg" 0.00 | cut -d'|' -f1)"
    [ "$_cov" = DARK ]    && { echo "  FAIL: a flat COVERED field must not classify DARK (the conflation bug)"; _fc_fail=1; }
    _dk="$(frame_class "$_fcdir/dark.jpg" 0.00 | cut -d'|' -f1)"
    [ "$_dk" = COVERED ]  && { echo "  FAIL: a noisy DARK room must not classify COVERED (sd discriminator broke)"; _fc_fail=1; }
    rm -rf "$_fcdir"
    [ "$_fc_fail" = 0 ] || { echo "smoke-test: FAIL"; exit 1; }
    # covered_overlay: SHUTTERED overlay + the >dwell ONE-shot [cam-covered] alert (hermetic — stub board+tg).
    _ovd="$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}"/cam-ov-XXXXXX)"
    COVSINCE="$_ovd/since"; INTENT_FLAG="$_ovd/intent"; CAM_COVERED_DWELL=3600; CAM_COVERED_TG=0
    CAMPOWER_STATE="$_ovd/campower"   # sandbox the EC-kill input too (the REAL node may be power=off right now)
    _bc="$_ovd/board"; cam_board(){ printf '%s\n' "$1" >> "$_bc"; }
    # (a) a fresh COVERED (since=now) is under dwell → returns COVERED, NO board post, arms the since-stamp
    rm -f "$_bc" "$COVSINCE"
    _e="$(covered_overlay COVERED)"; [ "$_e" = COVERED ] || { echo "  FAIL overlay: fresh COVERED must stay COVERED (got $_e)"; exit 1; }
    [ -s "$_bc" ] && { echo "  FAIL overlay: a sub-dwell COVERED must NOT post [cam-covered]"; exit 1; }
    # (b) backdate the since-stamp past the dwell → the NEXT overlay fires exactly ONE [cam-covered]
    printf '%s 0\n' "$(( $(date +%s) - 4000 ))" > "$COVSINCE"
    _e="$(covered_overlay COVERED)"; [ "$_e" = COVERED ] || { echo "  FAIL overlay: dwelled COVERED still reads COVERED (got $_e)"; exit 1; }
    [ "$(grep -c '\[cam-covered\]' "$_bc")" = 1 ] || { echo "  FAIL overlay: >dwell must post EXACTLY ONE [cam-covered] (got $(grep -c '\[cam-covered\]' "$_bc" 2>/dev/null))"; exit 1; }
    # (b') a further overlay in the SAME episode must NOT double-post (announced flag holds)
    _e="$(covered_overlay COVERED)"; [ "$(grep -c '\[cam-covered\]' "$_bc")" = 1 ] || { echo "  FAIL overlay: must not re-post within one covered episode"; exit 1; }
    # (c) a non-COVERED frame clears the episode (since-stamp removed) → re-arming is honest
    covered_overlay SEEING >/dev/null; [ -e "$COVSINCE" ] && { echo "  FAIL overlay: leaving COVERED must clear the dwell stamp"; exit 1; }
    # (d) operator-intent flag → COVERED renders SHUTTERED, no alert, no stamp churn
    : > "$INTENT_FLAG"; : > "$_bc"
    _e="$(covered_overlay COVERED)"; [ "$_e" = SHUTTERED ] || { echo "  FAIL overlay: intent flag must render SHUTTERED (got $_e)"; exit 1; }
    [ -s "$_bc" ] && { echo "  FAIL overlay: a SHUTTERED (intended) lens must not alarm"; exit 1; }
    # (e) EC privacy-kill (mesh-cam-power state 'off', FRESH) → COVERED renders SHUTTERED, no alarm —
    #     the cam-power↔cam-watch producer↔consumer link (Fn kill = operator intent, hardware edition)
    rm -f "$INTENT_FLAG"; : > "$_bc"; printf 'off\n' > "$CAMPOWER_STATE"
    _e="$(covered_overlay COVERED)"; [ "$_e" = SHUTTERED ] || { echo "  FAIL overlay: COVERED + fresh campower=off must render SHUTTERED (got $_e)"; exit 1; }
    [ -s "$_bc" ] && { echo "  FAIL overlay: an EC-killed lens must not alarm [cam-covered]"; exit 1; }
    # (e') STALE 'off' must NOT claim privacy-kill (honest-degrade: never silence a real covered alarm forever)
    touch -d '2 hours ago' "$CAMPOWER_STATE"
    _e="$(covered_overlay COVERED)"; [ "$_e" = COVERED ] || { echo "  FAIL overlay: STALE campower=off must not claim privacy-kill (got $_e)"; exit 1; }
    # (e'') power=on falsifies the gate the other way: a genuinely covered lens still reads COVERED
    printf 'on\n' > "$CAMPOWER_STATE"
    _e="$(covered_overlay COVERED)"; [ "$_e" = COVERED ] || { echo "  FAIL overlay: campower=on must leave COVERED alone (got $_e)"; exit 1; }
    rm -f "$CAMPOWER_STATE"
    unset -f cam_board; rm -rf "$_ovd"
    # operator-send throttle (2026-07-06): no stamp → due; fresh stamp → suppressed; >interval → due again.
    _tgd="$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}"/cam-tg-XXXXXX)"; TGSTAMP="$_tgd/.cam-last-tg"; CAM_TG_INTERVAL=3600
    tg_send_due && _a=DUE || _a=SUP; tg_stamp; tg_send_due && _b=DUE || _b=SUP
    echo "$(( $(date +%s) - 3601 ))" > "$TGSTAMP"; tg_send_due && _c=DUE || _c=SUP
    rm -rf "$_tgd"
    if [ "$_a" != DUE ] || [ "$_b" != SUP ] || [ "$_c" != DUE ]; then
      echo "  FAIL: tg throttle no-stamp=$_a(want DUE) fresh=$_b(want SUP) aged=$_c(want DUE)"; echo "smoke-test: FAIL"; exit 1
    fi
    # face-state artifact (gen-pair fusion, cam-watch × mesh-operator-home): every face-rec identity
    # read must land in the `-state`-named artifact (fleet-visible via mesh-fleet-states with zero
    # extra wiring) so a cross-node consumer can read "who was last seen here".
    _fsd="$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}"/cam-fs-XXXXXX)"; FACE_STATE="$_fsd/.cam-face-state"
    face_state_write "Ilya"
    [ "$(cat "$_fsd/.cam-face-state" 2>/dev/null)" = "Ilya" ] || { echo "  FAIL: face_state_write must persist the identity (got '$(cat "$_fsd/.cam-face-state" 2>/dev/null)')"; exit 1; }
    face_state_write "Nobody"
    [ "$(cat "$_fsd/.cam-face-state" 2>/dev/null)" = "Nobody" ] || { echo "  FAIL: face_state_write must overwrite, not append (got '$(cat "$_fsd/.cam-face-state" 2>/dev/null)')"; exit 1; }
    rm -rf "$_fsd"
    # --daemon singleton (chat-review/room-ambient-poke-churn 2026-07-10): a 2nd --daemon must EXIT at the
    # held lock, never stack a duplicate capture loop (room 11:11:52Z saw 3x running). Pre-hold the lock,
    # launch --daemon: it must return promptly (rc≠124), not loop until timeout. Falsify: drop the flock
    # guard → it enters the loop → timeout 124 → this assert fails.
    if command -v flock >/dev/null 2>&1; then
      _cwd="$(mktemp -d)"
      exec 9>"$_cwd/.cam-watch.daemon.lock"; flock -n 9 || { echo "smoke-test: FAIL (harness could not take cam-watch daemon lock)"; rm -rf "$_cwd"; exit 1; }
      MESH_DIR="$_cwd" timeout 4 bash "$0" --daemon >/dev/null 2>&1; _cwrc=$?
      flock -u 9 2>/dev/null; exec 9>&-
      [ "$_cwrc" = 124 ] && { echo "smoke-test: FAIL (2nd --daemon LOOPED past an already-held singleton lock — flock guard missing)"; rm -rf "$_cwd"; exit 1; }
      rm -rf "$_cwd"
      echo "  daemon singleton ok (2nd --daemon exits at held lock, no stacked capture loop)"
    fi
    echo "smoke-test: ok (diff metric + clip-gif assembly + 4 frame_class fixtures COVERED/DARK/FLAT/SEEING + split falsified both ways + covered_overlay dwell/once/reset/SHUTTERED + EC privacy-kill gate fresh/stale/on + tg-send throttle + face-state artifact + daemon-singleton)"
    ;;
  --noise)
    command -v fswebcam >/dev/null || { echo "no fswebcam"; exit 1; }
    echo "measuring static-scene diff over 6 frames (don't move in front of the camera)..."
    a="$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}"/n-XXXX.jpg)"; b="$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}"/n-XXXX.jpg)"; mx=0
    capture "$a" || { echo "capture fail"; exit 1; }
    for i in 1 2 3 4 5; do sleep "$CAM_POLL"; capture "$b" && { d="$(diff_metric "$a" "$b")"; echo "  frame $i: diff=$d"; cp -f "$b" "$a"; }; done
    rm -f "$a" "$b"
    echo "→ set CAM_THRESH a few points above the largest static diff above."
    ;;
  --clip-now)  # record a clip now and send it (manual verb + end-to-end verification of the video path)
    command -v fswebcam >/dev/null || { echo "no fswebcam"; exit 1; }
    who="?"
    [ "${CAM_VIDEO_CONFIRM:-0}" = 1 ] && who="$(person_present "$PREV" 2>/dev/null || echo '?')"
    clip="$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}"/cam-clip-XXXXXX.gif)"
    if record_clip "$clip"; then
      if send_animation "$clip" "👁 ${CAM_CAPTION:-clip} — $(date '+%H:%M:%S')${who:+ ($who)}"; then
        echo "clip sent ($(stat -c%s "$clip" 2>/dev/null) b)"; log_evt "VIDEO clip-now sent ($(stat -c%s "$clip" 2>/dev/null)b)"
      else echo "record ok, SEND FAILED — see $MESH/cam-curl.err"; rm -f "$clip"; exit 1; fi
    else echo "record FAILED (camera busy/absent?)"; rm -f "$clip"; exit 1; fi
    rm -f "$clip" ;;
  --shuttered)  # operator-intent flag: on = the closed shutter is intentional (COVERED→SHUTTERED, silenced)
    case "${2:-}" in
      on)  : > "$INTENT_FLAG" && echo "cam-watch: shutter marked INTENTIONAL — COVERED now renders SHUTTERED (alert silenced)" ;;
      off) rm -f "$INTENT_FLAG"; echo "cam-watch: shutter-intended cleared — a covered lens alarms again" ;;
      *)   [ -e "$INTENT_FLAG" ] && echo "shutter-intended: ON (covered lens renders SHUTTERED)" || echo "shutter-intended: off (a covered lens is COVERED and alarms after ${CAM_COVERED_DWELL}s)" ;;
    esac ;;
  --once)   cycle >/dev/null ;;
  --daemon)
    # SINGLETON (chat-review/room-ambient-poke-churn 2026-07-10): the systemd unit runs one instance, but
    # a MANUAL `mesh-cam-watch --daemon` re-launch used to stack a 2nd/3rd capture loop (room 11:11:52Z:
    # "3x duplicate mesh-cam-watch --daemon"). Each duplicate re-pokes the room mind on the same motion —
    # the --poke-mind flock (mesh-overhear) bounds concurrent pokes, but duplicate daemons still waste
    # capture cycles + double the .cam-motion stamp churn. A 2nd instance now exits at the lock. FAIL-OPEN
    # if flock is unavailable (never block the reflex on a missing coreutil).
    if command -v flock >/dev/null 2>&1; then
      exec 9>"$MESH/.cam-watch.daemon.lock"
      flock -n 9 || { log_evt "cam-watch: another --daemon holds the singleton lock — exiting (no stacking)"; exit 0; }
    fi
    log_evt "cam-watch START (dev=$CAM_DEV poll=${CAM_POLL}s thresh=$CAM_THRESH cooldown=${CAM_COOLDOWN}s)"
    while true; do cycle >/dev/null 2>&1 || true; sleep "$CAM_POLL"; done ;;
  *) sed -n '2,18p' "$0" ;;
esac
